// `@tier` is a known directive written at the wrong site: it decorates the `fn` that runs a tier,
// never a type. It reports E0054 (`InvalidDirectiveSite`) through the one placement check, like
// every other misplaced directive.
//
// It used to be an E0003 `UnexpectedToken` from the parser reading "unknown directive `@tier`" —
// a lie about a name the compiler knows, which sent the author hunting for a misspelling instead
// of moving the directive onto a function.
// expect: error E0054 at 10:2
// expect: exit 1
@tier(audit)
struct Report { lines: int }
echo "unreached"
